{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 52, :comments ["<b>And you shall dispossess, etc.</b> Now although the verse said concerning the seven nations (Deuteronomy 20:16) ״לֹא תְחַיֶּה כָּל נְשָׁמָה״, here the verse speaks of those other than the seven nations found there, and therefore it was precise in saying <b>all the inhabitants of the land</b>, to say: even if they are not of the seven nations." "Or it is possible that it refers back to a nation that does not have the power to kill them — rather, they should strive to dispossess them and not leave any of them in the land."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:17:03.623344783Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}